WEBVTT

00:00:13.598 --> 00:00:14.932
Care for a drink?

00:00:15.183 --> 00:00:18.186
I swiped it from the premier's cabinet.

00:00:18.436 --> 00:00:20.021
They'll send you to the boonies, you know.

00:00:20.271 --> 00:00:22.690
And you'll be right there with me.

00:00:25.151 --> 00:00:29.488
Who would've thought Ades soldiers
would end up fighting each other...

00:00:29.739 --> 00:00:34.994
How grief-stricken Augusta Farahnéz
would be if she were alive.

00:00:35.244 --> 00:00:39.832
Not even she was able to
put an end to the hatred;

00:00:40.082 --> 00:00:42.210
what hope do we commoners have?

00:00:43.794 --> 00:00:49.550
The premier will continue forward,
trampling friend and foe alike.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.429
Do you honestly think
there's a reason to continue

00:00:53.679 --> 00:00:56.015
after all these lives have been lost?

00:00:56.265 --> 00:00:59.560
If we defeat all of the opposition,
the fighting will end.

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:04.815
The premier is simply taking
the shortest path toward peace.

00:01:05.066 --> 00:01:07.485
The shortest path, huh...?

00:01:07.735 --> 00:01:12.031
Occasionally, I find myself terribly
envious of your matter-of-fact attitude.

00:01:18.079 --> 00:01:22.708
And I envy your zeal...

00:01:25.253 --> 00:01:31.842
<i>Soko ni nani ga aru toshite mo</i>

00:01:32.093 --> 00:01:40.518
<i>Mikai no ryouiki e kimi to</i>

00:01:48.776 --> 00:01:56.826
<i>Mijikai yume wo miteta ima</i>

00:01:57.076 --> 00:02:01.455
<i>Are wa kimi no senaka</i>

00:02:01.706 --> 00:02:07.628
<i>Kako? Mirai?</i>

00:02:07.878 --> 00:02:18.389
<i>Furikitte iru meetaa no hari wo mushi shite</i>

00:02:18.639 --> 00:02:21.517
<i>Oikaze to kanjou no muku hou e</i>

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:27.690
<i>Habataku tabi kizukasareru</i>

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:33.237
<i>Nido to deaenai sora ga aru koto</i>

00:02:33.487 --> 00:02:38.743
<i>Sore demo tobitatsu nara</i>

00:02:38.993 --> 00:02:45.541
<i>Kimi no tsubasa ni naru watashi ga</i>

00:03:05.269 --> 00:03:08.189
Twenty miles to Boreas Fortress.

00:03:08.439 --> 00:03:10.608
All hands, Type ll battle stations.

00:03:10.858 --> 00:03:13.027
All hands, Type ll battle stations!

00:03:14.278 --> 00:03:16.781
Bring the starboard-side guns around slowly!

00:03:19.241 --> 00:03:22.578
Oh! Are the aces of Kartoffel
finally heading into battle?

00:03:22.828 --> 00:03:25.831
You'll kick some butt for sure
with these at your disposal!

00:03:26.082 --> 00:03:29.251
We can fly just fine without 'em, though...

00:03:29.502 --> 00:03:31.462
No, you can't fight unarmed...!

00:03:31.712 --> 00:03:36.258
You guys took fifteen of our ships before!
This'll be a cinch for you!

00:03:36.509 --> 00:03:39.595
--But I don't wanna--
--C'mon! Just take it easy!

00:03:39.845 --> 00:03:44.392
We're here to defend the skies
and keep them free, right?

00:03:44.642 --> 00:03:47.311
Well, yeah, but...

00:03:47.561 --> 00:03:49.105
Fam.

00:03:50.231 --> 00:03:51.273
Enemy spotted!

00:03:51.524 --> 00:03:53.567
I repeat, enemy spotted!

00:03:53.818 --> 00:03:56.737
Approximately 100 ships 16 miles ahead.

00:03:56.987 --> 00:03:58.697
The 3rd and 4th Fleets.

00:03:58.948 --> 00:04:01.450
Firang and Sorfish...

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:04.412
There don't seem to be any
Turan ships among them.

00:04:04.662 --> 00:04:07.540
I appreciate your kind consideration, General.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:11.710
I realize you're going through
so much more than me.

00:04:11.961 --> 00:04:15.005
--Princess Millia...
--Signal flares from enemy fleets!

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:19.009
They wish to know our intent!

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:23.722
There is no room for negotiation.

00:04:23.973 --> 00:04:27.268
Augusta Farahnéz held fast to
the Ades Federation's aspiration

00:04:27.518 --> 00:04:29.854
for a world in which all
peoples can live in peace;

00:04:30.104 --> 00:04:33.816
a cause she then passed on to Augusta Sire-l.

00:04:34.066 --> 00:04:37.987
Yet, Luscinia continues
to trample upon that wish.

00:04:39.864 --> 00:04:43.534
And that's why you've so boorishly
brought the young Augusta Sire-l

00:04:43.784 --> 00:04:46.036
into the field of battle?

00:04:46.287 --> 00:04:50.833
We have taken a stand to
protect the Augusta's wish.

00:04:51.083 --> 00:04:53.836
"We"? You mean you.

00:04:54.086 --> 00:04:57.673
You would dare aim your guns at the Augusta?

00:04:57.923 --> 00:05:01.260
You're the one who's forced us
into this position, Vasant.

00:05:02.887 --> 00:05:04.847
Firang. What about you?

00:05:05.097 --> 00:05:08.058
I... No...

00:05:08.309 --> 00:05:14.523
That's too bad. I thought
you two would've understood.

00:05:14.773 --> 00:05:19.653
Our joint forces will commence
hostilities at 1200 hours.

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:28.162
Firang. This is our job, you know.

00:05:28.412 --> 00:05:32.583
Is it not our duty to protect the Augusta?

00:05:32.833 --> 00:05:36.670
Our duty is to lead the people to peace.

00:05:36.921 --> 00:05:37.963
But...

00:05:38.214 --> 00:05:42.259
The Augusta is really nothing more
than a representative of the people.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.553
If it comes down to it, she can be replaced.

00:05:44.803 --> 00:05:46.472
Sorfish!

00:05:46.722 --> 00:05:48.516
I'm only speaking hypothetically.

00:05:48.766 --> 00:05:52.770
For now, just focus on
accomplishing the task at hand.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:55.022
It's like Kayvén always says,

00:05:55.272 --> 00:06:00.277
"A soldier is a sword. Doubt will dull its blade."

00:06:05.324 --> 00:06:06.242
Marilla.

00:06:06.492 --> 00:06:09.495
There seems to be a lot of commotion outside...

00:06:09.745 --> 00:06:11.205
It's okay.

00:06:11.455 --> 00:06:19.338
General Vasant said your presence
here is for the sake of world peace.

00:06:23.634 --> 00:06:24.885
Boreas Fortress is a natural stronghold

00:06:25.135 --> 00:06:29.640
veiled in constant, thick fog
and surrounded by deep crevasses.

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:33.477
These crevasses exceed the
standard battleship altitude ceiling,

00:06:33.727 --> 00:06:37.398
leaving only these slabs of bedrock navigable.

00:06:37.648 --> 00:06:41.360
Stray from the rock and this will be the result...

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:44.947
Additionally, Boreas Fortress'
cannons pack quite a punch,

00:06:45.197 --> 00:06:49.076
and the only dead ground is this corridor here.

00:06:49.326 --> 00:06:52.621
In other words, we will make our push here.

00:06:52.871 --> 00:06:55.416
We can, of course, expect the
enemy to anticipate our move

00:06:55.666 --> 00:06:56.834
and form a battle array accordingly.

00:06:56.917 --> 00:06:58.961
...and form a battle array accordingly.

00:06:59.211 --> 00:07:01.797
We'll handle the 3rd Fleet.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.966
We'll handle the 3rd Fleet.

00:07:04.049 --> 00:07:08.679
They killed our brethren.
We will destroy them personally.

00:07:08.762 --> 00:07:12.850
They killed our brethren!
We will destroy them personally!

00:07:12.933 --> 00:07:15.227
I understand how you feel.

00:07:15.477 --> 00:07:21.025
But your Vanships are the only ones
that can withstand the 4th Fleet.

00:07:21.275 --> 00:07:22.026
But...!

00:07:22.276 --> 00:07:26.822
I ask that you take all of our
joint force into consideration.

00:07:28.741 --> 00:07:33.037
Please, I'm asking you to
handle the 4th Fleet instead.

00:07:36.707 --> 00:07:38.751
If we can evade the Federation's attack

00:07:39.001 --> 00:07:42.338
and get inside Boreas, victory will be ours.

00:07:42.588 --> 00:07:45.924
Please be mindful of the crevasses.

00:07:46.175 --> 00:07:47.301
All right. Got it.

00:07:47.551 --> 00:07:49.094
Rogen

00:07:50.596 --> 00:07:53.140
I think Fam is still a bit unsure about this.

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:54.475
Giselle...

00:07:54.725 --> 00:07:58.854
Fam and I want to protect these skies.
We want to protect Kartoffel.

00:07:59.104 --> 00:08:03.942
But we're Skyfish hunters, not soldiers.

00:08:04.193 --> 00:08:06.570
We've never shot at people before...

00:08:09.031 --> 00:08:14.703
Millia. When this fighting is over,
the world <i>will</i> be at peace, right?

00:08:14.953 --> 00:08:18.207
Yes. I have faith that it will.

00:08:20.125 --> 00:08:23.420
--We're heading out now, Princess Millia!
--Understood!

00:08:29.927 --> 00:08:31.470
You don't have to go, you know.

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:34.431
--Huh?
--Kartoffel is part of this fighting

00:08:34.682 --> 00:08:39.395
because of a past agreement
we made with Princess Liliana.

00:08:39.645 --> 00:08:46.276
And now we're working with Princess Millia
to defend the free skies from Luscinia.

00:08:46.527 --> 00:08:51.323
But that's only Kartoffel's decision.

00:08:51.573 --> 00:08:55.744
You have your own agreements you've made.

00:08:55.994 --> 00:08:59.039
Sky Pirates pride themselves
in keeping their word.

00:08:59.289 --> 00:09:03.252
It's that pride that gives us
free, unfettered wings.

00:09:03.502 --> 00:09:06.004
Atamora...

00:09:06.255 --> 00:09:08.507
Thanks. But I'm gonna go after all.

00:09:08.757 --> 00:09:11.176
I want to protect these skies too!

00:09:11.427 --> 00:09:12.886
Ah.

00:09:14.763 --> 00:09:18.225
3rd Joint Force Combat Squad in
position along western Boreas corridor!

00:09:18.475 --> 00:09:21.437
4th Combat Squad in position
along eastern corridor!

00:09:22.688 --> 00:09:24.064
It's time.

00:09:24.314 --> 00:09:26.400
Launch all Vanships!

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:28.277
All ships, 1st combat speed!

00:09:28.527 --> 00:09:31.155
Wipe out the Boreas traitors!

00:09:31.405 --> 00:09:33.532
All ships, 1st combat speed!

00:09:35.033 --> 00:09:37.494
All ships, scramble!

00:09:43.167 --> 00:09:46.879
--Can't we go any faster?
--This is the fastest we can go.

00:09:51.592 --> 00:09:56.305
I'm sure there are many here who
hold General Vasant in high regard.

00:09:58.348 --> 00:10:00.809
In fact, when I was young
I confessed my love to her,

00:10:01.059 --> 00:10:03.228
only to get the cold shoulder!

00:10:03.479 --> 00:10:07.775
But now we're fighting to recover the
Augusta from her traitorous clutches!

00:10:08.025 --> 00:10:09.985
This is a battle of honor!

00:10:10.235 --> 00:10:14.031
Put your feelings aside!
Destroy the enemy with all your might!

00:10:16.325 --> 00:10:19.620
All ships, 2nd combat speed!
Target the enemy flagship!

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:22.206
Understood! 2nd combat speed!

00:10:22.456 --> 00:10:24.416
Main enemy fleet has begun to move!

00:10:24.666 --> 00:10:26.460
All ships, prepare to open fire.

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:28.587
All ships, prepare to open fire!

00:10:30.088 --> 00:10:33.842
<i>Am I about to fire on the Augusta?</i>

00:10:36.345 --> 00:10:38.055
Can <i>I</i> really <i>do</i> that?

00:10:41.725 --> 00:10:45.312
Distance, 3,000. 2,500. 2,000.

00:10:45.395 --> 00:10:46.980
Enemy Vanships rapidly approaching!

00:10:47.231 --> 00:10:48.982
Prepare for counter-air combat!

00:10:49.066 --> 00:10:50.901
--800!
--Launch!

00:10:52.444 --> 00:10:54.404
--Fire!
--Fire!

00:11:03.205 --> 00:11:06.333
Five ships-of-the-line downed!
Four ships severely damaged!

00:11:06.583 --> 00:11:09.253
Glacies' new weapon, huh...?

00:11:09.503 --> 00:11:12.631
All ships, charge! Push them south!

00:11:14.258 --> 00:11:15.676
Man, they're fast!

00:11:15.926 --> 00:11:18.470
I don't like this anti-aircraft fire!

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:20.305
--Enemy ships above!
--Crap!

00:11:20.556 --> 00:11:22.391
G-Give us a break, will ya?!

00:11:24.518 --> 00:11:27.312
--Fam! Enemy at 5 o'clock!
--Roger!

00:11:28.856 --> 00:11:30.399
The steering's so heavy!

00:11:32.651 --> 00:11:34.820
--Within firing range!
--Roger!

00:11:41.368 --> 00:11:42.911
Fan'!

00:11:47.124 --> 00:11:48.625
No!

00:11:55.507 --> 00:11:57.009
You're emPtY!

00:11:58.468 --> 00:12:00.971
No, I can't do this after all...!

00:12:01.221 --> 00:12:03.223
This is insane!

00:12:04.433 --> 00:12:06.143
At this rate...

00:12:06.393 --> 00:12:09.563
...everyone's going to die!

00:12:13.984 --> 00:12:15.319
<i>What are you doing, Pam'?!</i>

00:12:15.569 --> 00:12:18.155
We're not soldiers!

00:12:22.868 --> 00:12:25.412
Orders to attack from the 4th Fleet.

00:12:25.662 --> 00:12:27.289
We're still out of firing range.

00:12:38.717 --> 00:12:40.177
Sorfish!

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:45.098
Is it true you asked to be
sent to the southern front?

00:12:45.349 --> 00:12:46.683
Yeah, it's true.

00:12:46.934 --> 00:12:50.312
That whole area's a battleground.
Do you want to die?

00:12:52.189 --> 00:12:54.983
A battlefield's a battlefield.

00:12:55.233 --> 00:12:58.195
I just figure it'd be fun to go
where the most action--

00:12:58.445 --> 00:12:59.821
and glory-- might be.

00:13:00.072 --> 00:13:05.661
I guess I, uh, expected you
to take the easy way out.

00:13:05.911 --> 00:13:08.372
You were never serious during training,

00:13:08.622 --> 00:13:11.458
and you don't seem all that loyal to the Augusta.

00:13:11.708 --> 00:13:15.963
How mean. I admire Augusta
Farahnéz too, you know.

00:13:16.213 --> 00:13:18.298
Seriously, she is pretty and all!

00:13:18.548 --> 00:13:20.968
Don't disrespect the Augusta!

00:13:21.218 --> 00:13:23.178
I bet you became a soldier

00:13:23.428 --> 00:13:29.059
because you have genuine faith in
her ideals and in Ades' future, huh?

00:13:29.309 --> 00:13:30.811
Didn't you?

00:13:31.061 --> 00:13:34.982
No. I was just... envious.

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:38.110
I don't know what that means.

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:42.572
It's nothing. Just follow your own path.

00:13:42.823 --> 00:13:47.035
Maybe sometimes I'll bother
to keep an eye on you.

00:13:47.285 --> 00:13:49.663
That's not very encouraging, actually.

00:13:51.415 --> 00:13:54.543
They're sending you to the east, right?

00:13:54.793 --> 00:13:57.295
The east is almost as intense
a battleground as the south.

00:13:57.546 --> 00:13:59.006
Yeah.

00:14:00.632 --> 00:14:03.218
Let's swear to meet again here, in the capital.

00:14:03.468 --> 00:14:05.762
Gloria, Augusta.

00:14:07.931 --> 00:14:11.393
<i>Back then, I had no uncertainty whatsoever.</i>

00:14:11.643 --> 00:14:16.732
My <i>only concern was for
the Augusta, for Ades' future...</i>

00:14:19.651 --> 00:14:21.486
But, now...

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:27.367
1st Combat Squad entering southern corridor!

00:14:27.617 --> 00:14:30.078
4th Fleet moving south!

00:14:30.328 --> 00:14:32.497
(Drang is acting odd.

00:14:32.748 --> 00:14:35.000
Is he worried about the altitude ceiling issue?

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:36.877
No, wait...

00:14:37.127 --> 00:14:38.545
2nd and 3rd Combat Squads,

00:14:38.795 --> 00:14:42.549
flank both sides while keeping your distance!

00:14:42.799 --> 00:14:45.802
2, 3. It's your turn, Augusta Sire-l.

00:14:46.053 --> 00:14:47.345
Those sounds...

00:14:47.596 --> 00:14:52.517
Don't worry. Lady Vasant will
destroy the enemy if they come.

00:14:52.768 --> 00:14:56.646
What enemy? ls Luscinia here?

00:14:56.897 --> 00:14:59.149
Or is it one of the generals?!

00:14:59.399 --> 00:15:01.485
Umm, I'm afraid I don't know...

00:15:01.735 --> 00:15:03.695
Why must everyone fight?!

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:08.116
They all got along so well before...

00:15:08.366 --> 00:15:11.703
Why...? Why, why?!

00:15:15.624 --> 00:15:18.335
--What's the prey?
--The fastest one!

00:15:18.585 --> 00:15:20.962
The 4th Fleet's high-speed, heavy flotilla leader

00:15:21.213 --> 00:15:22.798
commanded by General Sorfish...

00:15:23.048 --> 00:15:25.884
The Senapati, huh?

00:15:26.134 --> 00:15:27.094
Listen up, men!

00:15:27.344 --> 00:15:30.555
Our prey's fast and big! Look alive!

00:15:32.432 --> 00:15:34.434
Focus only on reaching the Augusta.

00:15:34.684 --> 00:15:38.146
They've nowhere to run now,
anyway. Push forward!

00:15:45.779 --> 00:15:48.115
Enemy ship dead ahead!
It's preparing to ram us!

00:15:48.365 --> 00:15:50.867
Emergency ascent! Let it pass--!

00:15:57.541 --> 00:16:00.961
--Hard aport!
--Hard aport!

00:16:01.211 --> 00:16:04.923
We're not going to make it!
We've lost buoyancy! We're falling!

00:16:12.556 --> 00:16:16.101
Watch that altitude ceiling!
Don't let the enemy overpower us!

00:16:22.315 --> 00:16:24.860
--Target located!
--Let's do it, guys!

00:16:29.573 --> 00:16:31.158
Sky Pirate Vanships approaching!

00:16:31.408 --> 00:16:34.202
The ones who gave (Drang a good scare, huh?

00:16:38.665 --> 00:16:40.333
First harpoon!

00:16:55.098 --> 00:16:56.016
Did we get it?!

00:16:56.266 --> 00:16:57.934
Full speed ahead!

00:17:02.355 --> 00:17:04.274
It didn't work!

00:17:04.524 --> 00:17:07.652
They'll have to do better than that to stop me.

00:17:07.903 --> 00:17:10.780
Forward! The Augusta isn't far now!

00:17:20.916 --> 00:17:23.293
The Augusta's flag...!

00:17:25.003 --> 00:17:27.714
You would fire on the Augusta?!

00:17:30.508 --> 00:17:34.721
Lowly traitor. I can't stand
to see you fly her flag.

00:17:34.971 --> 00:17:36.473
Send up the signal flares!

00:17:38.892 --> 00:17:41.603
Orders to attack from the 4th Fleet!

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:48.276
The premier is simply taking
the shortest path toward peace.

00:17:51.071 --> 00:17:56.117
<i>I</i> truly envy that matter-of-fact attitude of yours.

00:17:56.368 --> 00:17:57.953
But...

00:17:58.203 --> 00:17:59.704
Sorfish...

00:18:01.915 --> 00:18:04.042
All ships, prepare to open fire!

00:18:07.295 --> 00:18:09.881
Evasive action! Do not let them approach!

00:18:11.925 --> 00:18:15.220
We need only recover the
Augusta to end this battle.

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:18.265
All hands, prepare for hand-to-hand combat!

00:18:18.515 --> 00:18:23.019
--What's happening?!
--The 3rd Fleet's Admiraly is firing on us!

00:18:26.898 --> 00:18:30.360
We are loyal vassals to the Augusta!

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:32.862
I will permit no further atrocities!

00:18:33.113 --> 00:18:34.572
C_)rang...

00:18:34.823 --> 00:18:37.367
Direct hit to upper sub-bridge!

00:18:37.617 --> 00:18:38.827
Aft thruster has been hit!

00:18:39.077 --> 00:18:42.455
So this is the path you've chosen...

00:18:47.419 --> 00:18:48.920
I don't know why...

00:18:51.006 --> 00:18:56.928
...but I always had the
feeling this day would come.

00:18:57.178 --> 00:18:59.306
Follow your own path.

00:19:01.683 --> 00:19:03.768
But, as for me...

00:19:07.731 --> 00:19:09.190
Attention, all ships!

00:19:09.441 --> 00:19:11.985
All who follow the Augusta, surrender at once!

00:19:12.235 --> 00:19:13.862
Those who wish for true peace,

00:19:14.112 --> 00:19:17.574
seek out the premier once you've
broken through the enemy forces!

00:19:19.576 --> 00:19:21.953
The Senapati is launching a
suicide attack on the Augusta's ship!

00:19:23.288 --> 00:19:25.332
All ships, fire!

00:19:34.674 --> 00:19:36.718
Sorry to drag you into this.

00:19:36.968 --> 00:19:39.471
Not at all. This is nothing new to me.

